{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 as a persistent passive-FTP destination for the scanner account. The account is confined to a dedicated dropbox, anonymous access is disabled, access is firewalled to node2, and both nodes passed sequential restart and recovery verification.","actions_performed":["Installed the CentOS Stream 10 repository version of vsftpd without changing the OS release or kernel.","Created the non-shell scanner account from the staged handover and configured its chrooted dropbox.","Enabled passive FTP on TCP 30000–30009 with SELinux and firewalld persistence.","Uploaded and retrieved the supplied sample scan byte-for-byte from node2; also retrieved the existing received document.","Verified anonymous rejection and denial of files outside the dropbox before and after restarting both nodes sequentially."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Passive FTP upload destination and scanner account","command_ids":["cmd-51d114965106461d","cmd-58065e24c9a44e74","cmd-9e37614ea42e4687"],"summary":"Shows the configured service, scanner-only account, chroot location, active listener, final package version, and successful sample upload/retrieval."},{"requirement":"Passive-mode operation","command_ids":["cmd-4adbb71b557343c1","cmd-bbd2290d58514de8"],"summary":"EPSV selected TCP 30009 and completed retrieval; passive upload and byte-identical retrieval also succeeded after both restarts."},{"requirement":"Dropbox confinement and anonymous access disabled","command_ids":["cmd-3aea97537d574757","cmd-d473048b2d534a15","cmd-9e37614ea42e4687"],"summary":"Anonymous authentication returns FTP 530, attempts to access sibling and host files fail, and final configuration confirms anonymous disabled with a chrooted non-shell account."},{"requirement":"Existing OS release and kernel retained","command_ids":["cmd-0cf913a5df4347b2","cmd-55ac5db51b5f4e66","cmd-9e37614ea42e4687","cmd-bbd2290d58514de8"],"summary":"Both nodes remain on CentOS Stream 10 with kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 before and after configuration and restarts."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-f12868e4165e44c4","cmd-cf5222fe068548a0","cmd-c0f2d601af1146f6","cmd-8541b5119156427b","cmd-db656bbdc450494f","cmd-18a4ae097bcb4e92"],"summary":"Captures the healthy baseline, acknowledged reboot, temporary unavailability, changed boot ID, recovered service/policy/data, and successful remote retrieval."},{"requirement":"Node2 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-0dba49233b2f4008","cmd-81972976cdb64e55","cmd-45744fdbd566458f","cmd-a568ba73ea404bac","cmd-bbd2290d58514de8"],"summary":"Captures the healthy baseline, acknowledged reboot, temporary unavailability, changed boot ID, intact staged data, and recovered passive upload/retrieval."}]}
